H7300.definition:
a primitive root;
to tramp about, i.e. ramble (free or disconsolate)
KJV: have the dominion, be lord, mourn, rule.

H7301.definition:
a primitive root;
to slake the thirst (occasionally of other appetites)
KJV: bathe, make drunk, (take the) fill, satiate, (abundantly) satisfy, soak, water (abundantly).

H7302.definition:
from H7301 (רָוָה);
sated (with drink)
KJV: drunkenness, watered.

H7303.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to cry out; outcry;
Rohagah, an Israelite
KJV: Rohgah.

H7304.definition:
a primitive root (identical with H7306 (רוּחַ));
properly, to breathe freely, i.e. revive; by implication, to have ample room
KJV: be refreshed, large.

H7305.definition:
from H7304 (רָוַח);
room, literally (an interval) or figuratively (deliverance)
KJV: enlargement, space.

H7306.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to blow, i.e. breathe; only (literally) to smell or (by implication, perceive (figuratively, to anticipate, enjoy)
KJV: accept, smell, [idiom] touch, make of quick understanding.

H7307.definition:
from H7306 (רוּחַ);
wind; by resemblance breath, i.e. a sensible (or even violent) exhalation; figuratively, life, anger, unsubstantiality; by extension, a region of the sky; by resemblance spirit, but only of a rational being (including its expression and functions)
KJV: air, anger, blast, breath, [idiom] cool, courage, mind, [idiom] quarter, [idiom] side, spirit(-ual), tempest, [idiom] vain, (whirl-) wind(-y).

H7308.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7307 (רוּחַ)
{wind; by resemblance breath, i.e. a sensible (or even violent) exhalation; figuratively, life, anger, unsubstantiality; by extension, a region of the sky; by resemblance spirit, but only of a rational being (including its expression and functions)}
KJV: mind, spirit, wind.

H7309.definition:
feminine of H7305 (רֶוַח);
relief
KJV: breathing, respite.

H7310.definition:
from H7301 (רָוָה);
satisfaction
KJV: runneth over, wealthy.

H7311.definition:
a primitive root;
to be high actively, to rise or raise (in various applications, literally or figuratively)
KJV: bring up, exalt (self), extol, give, go up, haughty, heave (up), (be, lift up on, make on, set up on, too) high(-er, one), hold up, levy, lift(-er) up, (be) lofty, ([idiom] a-) loud, mount up, offer (up), [phrase] presumptuously, (be) promote(-ion), proud, set up, tall(-er), take (away, off, up), breed worms.

H7312.definition:
or רֻם; from H7311 (רוּם);
(literally) elevation or (figuratively) elation
KJV: haughtiness, height, [idiom] high.

H7313.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7311 (רוּם);
{to be high actively, to rise or raise (in various applications, literally or figuratively)}
KJV: extol, lift up (self), set up.

H7315.definition:
from H7311 (רוּם);
elevation, i.e. (adverbially) aloft
KJV: on high.

H7316.definition:
from H7311 (רוּם); height;
Rumah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Rumah.

H7317.definition:
feminine of H7315 (רוֹם);
elation, i.e. (adverbially) proudly
KJV: haughtily.

H7318.definition:
from H7426 (רָמַם);
exaltation, i.e. (figuratively and specifically) praise
KJV: be extolled.

H7319.definition:
feminine active participle of H7426 (רָמַם);
exaltation, i.e. praise
KJV: high.

H7320.definition:
(or Romam from H7311 (רוּם) and H5828 (עֵזֶר); I have raised up a help;
Romamti-Ezer, an Israelite
KJV: Romamti-ezer.

H7321.definition:
a primitive root;
to mar (especially by breaking); figuratively, to split the ears (with sound), i.e. shout (for alarm or joy)
KJV: blow an alarm, cry (alarm, aloud, out), destroy, make a joyful noise, smart, shout (for joy), sound an alarm, triumph.

H7322.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to triturate (in a mortar), i.e. (figuratively) to agitate (by concussion)
KJV: tremble.

H7323.definition:
a primitive root;
to run (for whatever reason, especially to rush)
KJV: break down, divide speedily, footman, guard, bring hastily, (make) run (away, through), post.

H7324.definition:
a primitive root;
to pour out (literally or figuratively), i.e. empty
KJV: [idiom] arm, cast out, draw (out), (make) empty, pour forth (out).

H7325.definition:
a primitive root;
to slaver (with spittle), i.e. (by analogy) to emit afluid (ulcerous or natural)
KJV: run.

H7326.definition:
a primitive root;
to be destitute
KJV: lack, needy, (make self) poor (man).

H7327.definition:
probably for H7468 (רְעוּת); friend;
Ruth, a Moabitess
KJV: Ruth.

H7329.definition:
a primitive root;
to emaciate, i.e. make (become) thin (literally or figuratively)
KJV: famish, wax lean.

H7331.definition:
from H7336 (רָזַן); prince;
Rezon, a Syrian
KJV: Rezon.

H7332.definition:
from H7329 (רָזָה);
thinness
KJV: leanness, [idiom] scant.

H7333.definition:
from H7336 (רָזַן);
a dignitary
KJV: prince.

H7335.definition:
a primitive root;
to twinkle the eye (in mockery)
KJV: wink.

H7336.definition:
a primitive root;
probably to be heavy, i.e. (figuratively) honorable
KJV: prince, ruler.

H7337.definition:
a primitive root;
to broaden (intransitive or transitive, literal or figurative)
KJV: be an en-(make) large(-ing), make room, make (open) wide.

H7338.definition:
from H7337 (רָחַב);
a width
KJV: breadth, broad place.

H7339.definition:
or רְחוֹב; from H7337 (רָחַב);
a width, i.e. (concretely) avenue or area
KJV: broad place (way), street. See also H1050 (בֵּית רְחוֹב).

H7340.definition:
or רְחוֹב; the same as H7339 (רְחֹב);
Rechob, the name of a place in Syria, also of a Syrian and an Israelite
KJV: Rehob.

H7341.definition:
from H7337 (רָחַב);
width (literally or figuratively)
KJV: breadth, broad, largeness, thickness, wideness.

H7342.definition:
from H7337 (רָחַב);
roomy, in any (or every) direction, literally or figuratively
KJV: broad, large, at liberty, proud, wide.

H7343.definition:
the same as H7342 (רָחָב); proud;
Rachab, a Canaanitess
KJV: Rahab.

H7344.definition:
or רְחֹבֹת; plural of H7339 (רְחֹב); streets;
Rechoboth, a place in Assyria and one in Palestine
KJV: Rehoboth.

H7345.definition:
or רְחַבְיָהוּ; from H7337 (רָחַב) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has enlarged;
Rechabjah, an Israelite
KJV: Rehabiah.

H7346.definition:
from H7337 (רָחַב) and H5971 (עַם); a people has enlarged;
Rechabam, an Israelite king
KJV: Rehoboam.

H7347.definition:
from an unused root meaning to pulverize;
a mill-stone
KJV: mill (stone).

H7348.definition:
a form of H7349 (רַחוּם);
Rechum, the name of a Persian and of three Israelites
KJV: Rehum.

H7349.definition:
from H7355 (רָחַם);
compassionate
KJV: full of compassion, merciful.

H7350.definition:
or רָחֹק; from H7368 (רָחַק);
remote, literally or figuratively, of place or time; specifically, precious; often used adverbially (with preposition)
KJV: (a-) far (abroad, off), long ago, of old, space, great while to come.

H7351.definition:
from the same as H7298 (רַהַט);
a panel (as resembling a trough)
KJV: rafter.

H7352.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7350 (רָחוֹק)
{remote, literally or figuratively, of place or time; specifically, precious; often used adverbially (with preposition)}
KJV: far.

H7353.definition:
from an unused root meaning to journey;
a ewe (the females being the predominant element of a flock) (as a good traveller)
KJV: ewe, sheep.

H7354.definition:
the same as H7353 (רָחֵל);
Rachel, a wife of Jacob
KJV: Rachel.

H7355.definition:
a primitive root;
to fondle; by implication, to love, especially to compassionate
KJV: have compassion (on, upon), love, (find, have, obtain, shew) mercy(-iful, on, upon), (have) pity, Ruhamah, [idiom] surely.

H7356.definition:
from H7355 (רָחַם);
compassion (in the plural); by extension, the womb (as cherishing the fetus); by implication, a maiden
KJV: bowels, compassion, damsel, tender love, (great, tender) mercy, pity, womb.

H7357.definition:
the same as H7356 (רַחַם); pity;
Racham, an Israelite
KJV: Raham.

H7358.definition:
from H7355 (רָחַם); (compare H7356 (רַחַם))
the womb
KJV: matrix, womb.

H7359.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7356 (רַחַם);
(plural) pity
KJV: mercy.

H7360.definition:
or (feminine) רָחָמָה; from H7355 (רָחַם);
a kind of vulture (supposed to be tender towards its young)
KJV: gier-eagle.

H7361.definition:
feminine of H7356 (רַחַם);
a maiden
KJV: damsel.

H7363.definition:
a primitive root;
to brood; by implication, to be relaxed
KJV: flutter, move, shake.

H7364.definition:
a primitive root;
to lave (the whole or a part of a thing)
KJV: bathe (self), wash (self).

H7365.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7364 (רָחַץ) (probably through the accessory idea of ministering as a servant at the bath);
to attend upon
KJV: trust.

H7366.definition:
from H7364 (רָחַץ);
a bath
KJV: wash(-pot).

H7367.definition:
feminine of H7366 (רַחַץ);
a bathing place
KJV: washing.

H7368.definition:
a primitive root;
to widen (in any direction), i.e. (intransitively) recede or (transitively) remove (literally or figuratively, of place or relation)
KJV: (a-, be, cast, drive, get, go, keep (self), put, remove, be too, (wander), withdraw) far (away, off), loose, [idiom] refrain, very, (be) a good way (off).

H7369.definition:
from H7368 (רָחַק);
remote
KJV: that are far.

H7370.definition:
a primitive root;
to gush
KJV: indite.

H7371.definition:
from H7306 (רוּחַ);
a winnowing-fork (as blowing the chaff away)
KJV: shovel.

H7372.definition:
a primitive root;
to be moist
KJV: be wet.

H7373.definition:
from H7372 (רָטַב);
moist (with sap)
KJV: green.

H7374.definition:
from an unused root meaning to tremble;
terror
KJV: fear.

H7375.definition:
a root compounded from H7373 (רָטֹב) and H2954 (טָפַשׁ);
to be rejuvenated
KJV: be fresh.

H7376.definition:
a primitive root;
to dash down
KJV: dash (in pieces).

H7377.definition:
from H7301 (רָוָה);
irrigation, i.e. a shower
KJV: watering.

H7378.definition:
or רוּב; a primitive root;
properly, to toss, i.e. grapple; mostly figuratively, to wrangle, i.e. hold a controversy; (by implication) to defend
KJV: adversary, chide, complain, contend, debate, [idiom] ever, [idiom] lay wait, plead, rebuke, strive, [idiom] thoroughly.

H7379.definition:
or רִב; from H7378 (רִיב);
a contest (personal or legal)
KJV: [phrase] adversary, cause, chiding, contend(-tion), controversy, multitude (from the margin), pleading, strife, strive(-ing), suit.

H7380.definition:
from H7378 (רִיב); contentious;
Ribai, an Israelite
KJV: Ribai.

H7381.definition:
from H7306 (רוּחַ);
odor (as if blown)
KJV: savour, scent, smell.

H7382.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7381 (רֵיחַ)
{odor (as if blown)}
KJV: smell.

H7383.definition:
or רִפָה; from H7322 (רוּף);
(only plural), grits (as pounded)
KJV: ground corn, wheat.

H7384.definition:
or (probably by orthographical error) דִּיפַת; of foreign origin;
Riphath, a grandson of Japheth and his descendants
KJV: Riphath.

H7385.definition:
from H7324 (רוּק);
emptiness; figuratively, a worthless thing; adverbially, in vain
KJV: empty, to no purpose, (in) vain (thing), vanity.

H7386.definition:
or (shorter) רֵק; from H7324 (רוּק);
empty; figuratively, worthless
KJV: emptied(-ty), vain (fellow, man).

H7387.definition:
from H7386 (רֵיק);
emptily; figuratively (objective) ineffectually, (subjective) undeservedly
KJV: without cause, empty, in vain, void.

H7388.definition:
from H7325 (רוּר);
saliva; by resemblance, broth
KJV: spittle, white (of an egg).

H7389.definition:
or רֵאשׁ; or רִישׁ; from H7326 (רוּשׁ);
poverty
KJV: poverty.

H7390.definition:
from H7401 (רָכַךְ);
tender (literally or figuratively); by implication, weak
KJV: faint((-hearted), soft, tender ((-hearted), one), weak.

H7392.definition:
a primitive root;
to ride (on an animal or in a vehicle); causatively, to place upon (for riding or generally), to despatch
KJV: bring (on (horse-) back), carry, get (oneself) up, on (horse-) back, put, (cause to, make to) ride (in a chariot, on, -r), set.

H7393.definition:
from H7392 (רָכַב);
a vehicle; by implication, a team; by extension, cavalry; by analogy a rider, i.e. the upper millstone
KJV: chariot, (upper) millstone, multitude (from the margin), wagon.

H7394.definition:
from H7392 (רָכַב); rider;
Rekab, the name of two Arabs and of two Israelites
KJV: Rechab.

H7395.definition:
from H7392 (רָכַב);
a charioteer
KJV: chariot man, driver of a chariot, horseman.

H7396.definition:
feminine of H7393 (רֶכֶב);
a chariot (collectively)
KJV: chariots.

H7397.definition:
probably feminine from H7401 (רָכַךְ); softness;
Rekah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Rechah.

H7398.definition:
from passive participle of H7392 (רָכַב);
a vehicle (as ridden on)
KJV: chariot.

H7399.definition:
or רְכֻשׁ; from passive participle of H7408 (רָכַשׁ);
property (as gathered)
KJV: good, riches, substance.
